# Documentation and Evidence Ownership

Use `docs/DOCUMENTATION-ORGANIZATION.md` to choose the owner before creating or
moving a file.

- Give each document one primary job.
- Link to canonical status instead of duplicating volatile observations.
- Preserve dated evidence; use an appended dated addendum for later
  interpretation.
- Treat `evidence/kagent/README.md` as the current kagent status owner.
- Keep review reports non-authoritative.
- Add every new canonical repository artifact to `REPO_MANIFEST.yaml`; never
  map generated, ignored, or temporary output.
- Assess every affected owner independently. An unchanged earlier owner does
  not imply later owners can be skipped.
- Run applicable link, manifest, and format checks before reporting completion.
- Do not create a competing roadmap, status ledger, capability matrix, or
  documentation-placement guide.
